+ * checked once with a probe entry, at init when the table is empty and
+ * nothing can match it: a hash-mode add of a nine-word entry must land at
+ * an even index, that slot must then read valid and the one after it
+ * must not read as a valid head, and after an index-mode delete both
+ * slots must read empty. The probe keys an unspecified address and zero
+ * ports against host and nexthop index 0, which no packet resolves to.
+ * Any other outcome leaves IPv6 on the software path (declined once
+ * per reason) rather than trusting slot arithmetic that hardware does
+ * not share.
